<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sour-starter" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Sourdough Starter </title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell>Flour</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>Water</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Days 1, 2, 3, 4, &amp; 5:  In the morning, add about <m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup flour and enough water to make a thick batter.  Stir vigorously.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          This process works best when the temperature is relatively warm (at least <m>67^\circ</m>).  When it is colder, the yeast needs an extra day to grow.  So I reduce the flour to <m>\frac{1}{4}</m> cup on days 2 &amp; 3 and add another <m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup on day 6.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Used in <alert>Whole Wheat Sourdough Bread</alert> and <alert>Sourdough Pancakes &amp; Waffles</alert>
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>